lean-hedgehog NEWS -- history of user-visible changes.

0.2.0 (unreleased)

  - Coverage: classify, cover, label and collect count the kinds of
    test case a property names, and the report lists each with its
    percentage.  A property whose tests pass fails when a kind stays
    below the minimum that cover asks for.
  - scenario takes a range of lengths for madhouse mode and a setup
    that runs before the first command.  scenarioFrom generates the
    start state, which no longer needs a default.
  - USAGE says that Gen.sequence shrinks by removing elements.
  - Incompatible: Log has the constructor label, Status the constructor
    uncovered, and Report the field coverage.  A match on Log or
    Status needs the new case, and ⟨tests, discards, status⟩ a fourth
    component.

0.1.0 (2026-11-18)

  - Generators with integrated shrinking: Gen, Range, Seed, Tree.
    Numbers, booleans, characters, strings, lists, arrays, options,
    choice, frequency, recursion, filtering, subsequences, shuffles.
  - Properties: property and propertyM, forAll, ===, /==, ensure,
    annotate, tripping, discard, evalIO.
  - A runner: check, recheck, checkGroup, and Property.report, which
    is a pure function for a pure property.
  - Hedgehog.StateMachine: model-based testing with transitions as one
    type, after proptest-state-machine.
  - Hedgehog.Command: model-based testing with commands as types and a
    MADHOUSE=1 mode, after madhouse-rs.
  - LawfulMonad Tree is a theorem.
  - Not ported yet: coverage (classify, cover, label), symbolic
    variables and parallel state machine testing, floating-point
    generators, diffs of the two sides of ===, test discovery.
